### Python ###
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg

### Generated project data — reproducible via pipeline/generate_wallet_profiles.py ###
data/wallet_profiles.csv
*.snappy.parquet

### ML model artifacts — reproducible via pipeline/train_isolation_forest.py ###
models/isoforest_model.joblib
models/isoforest_model_meta.json

### Runtime state — all reproducible by running the pipeline; this whole
### folder is generated, nothing in it should ever be committed.
runtime/*
!runtime/.gitkeep

### Neo4j local state ###
# docker-compose.yml's named volumes (neo4j_data/neo4j_logs) live inside
# Docker, not the repo, but guard against anyone bind-mounting locally.
neo4j-data/
neo4j-logs/

### Spark local state ###
spark-warehouse/
metastore_db/
derby.log

### Ivy / Maven dependency resolution (spark.jars.packages) ###
# Matches graph_storage.py / streaming_engine.py's dynamic package resolution
# writing to C:\Users\<user>\.ivy2 — only relevant if that cache ever ends up
# inside the repo directory instead of the user profile.
.ivy2/
ivy-cache/

### Hadoop on Windows ###
# C:\hadoop\logs referenced in graph_storage.py's os.makedirs() call —
# only matters if C:\hadoop ever ends up nested under the repo.
hadoop/logs/
winutils.exe

### Docker ###
# No compose overrides are currently tracked separately, but ignore local
# override files if you ever add one for machine-specific tweaks.
docker-compose.override.yml

### IDE / OS noise ###
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

### Kafka (if ever run with a local, non-Docker broker) ###
kafka-logs/
zookeeper-data/

### Secrets ###
# graph_storage.py loads NEO4J_PASSWORD from this via python-dotenv —
# copy .env.example to .env locally, never commit the real file.
.env
.env.local
